		{"id":"ec09f3d896874fb2","type":"file","file":"Data/0PAPER/LeakageTunneling/InSubspace/OffResonance211/Heatmap/wide.png","x":1440,"y":6600,"width":400,"height":267,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1e666c5ade9f5bd9","type":"file","file":"Data/0PAPER/LeakageTunneling/InSubspace/OffResonance211/DetuningHeatmap/RelativeFreq/heatmap_max_amps.png","x":1840,"y":6600,"width":400,"height":267,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"3cff21e62161c004","type":"text","text":"The anharmonicity is assumed to be 300 here, does it matter?","x":1035,"y":7120,"width":250,"height":109},
		{"id":"0d6bdc8dcc0c9ef8","type":"text","text":"It is assumed that the couplings are the same here, does it matter?","x":1513,"y":7120,"width":244,"height":85},
		{"id":"1655170d646ab38d","type":"text","text":"Show in appendix it doesn't matter.","x":1035,"y":7309,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5c8b6adac63cc52a","type":"text","text":"The couplings can change the off-position for the zz coupling, for the couplers. This then changes their frequency obviously, causing more detuning. It can matter?","x":1501,"y":7309,"width":269,"height":185},
