		{"id":"08d2dc991480ffe7","type":"file","file":"Data/0PAPER/LeakageTunneling/200.png","x":-1174,"y":4144,"width":400,"height":267,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d4aab9cd2c8948ec","type":"text","text":"Here the parameters are little different. $w_1 = w_3 = 3.75 \\textrm{GHz}$. But anyways, it seems like we have similar leakage mobility as in the $g = 0$ case, but just slower.\n\nI used the same ZZ-off position here as in just the two qubit case. I would case they \"real\" ZZ-off here might be slightly different, but I don't expect it to change the results.","x":-1620,"y":4196,"width":315,"height":484,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"834d57232049baf8","type":"file","file":"Data/0PAPER/LeakageTunneling/InSubspace/OffResonance211/Heatmap/furtherZoom.png","x":2180,"y":4614,"width":220,"height":147},
